Pre-commit check results:
  ~~~
  epan/dissectors/packet-srt.c:  FT_BOOLEAN:       proto_tree_add_item(tree, hf_srt_km_sign, tvb, baseoff + 1, 2, [[ENC_BIG_ENDIAN]-->[ENC_NA]]);
epan/dissectors/packet-srt.c:  FT_BOOLEAN:       proto_tree_add_item(tree, hf_srt_km_salt, tvb, baseoff + 16, slen, [[ENC_BIG_ENDIAN]-->[ENC_NA]]);
epan/dissectors/packet-srt.c:  FT_BOOLEAN:       proto_tree_add_item(tree, hf_srt_km_wrap, tvb, baseoff + wrap_offset, blocklen - wrap_offset, [[ENC_BIG_ENDIAN]-->[ENC_NA]]);

If I use `proto_tree_add_bitmask`, do I have to combine the fields into some group?
E.g. rewriting the code this way requires me to create some group, while there is no group defined by the protocol spec:
```c++
static int* const first_byte[] = {
        & hf_srt_km_s,
        & hf_srt_km_v,
        & hf_srt_km_pt,
        NULL
    };

u8bits = tvb_get_guint8(tvb, baseoff);
proto_tree_add_bitmask(tree, tvb, baseoff, hf_srt_km_flags, 0, first_byte, ENC_BIG_ENDIAN);


{&hf_srt_km_flags, {
    "KM Flags", "srt.km.flags",
    FT_UINT8, BASE_DEC, NULL,
    0, NULL, HFILL}},
```

